  "notes": "University Park. Built from the real archived 2025-26 bulletin (raw HTML fetched directly, not WebFetch's summarizer). This is the first fully-merged catalog year: unlike 2022/2023/2024 (which still split into the separate 'Environmental Systems Engineering Option' and 'Environmental Health and Safety Option', see ENVSYS-2022/2023/2024.json's notes), the Spring-2025 curricular update (first documented on the 2024-25 archived page's own 'Spring 2025 Curricular Update' banner) is now the ONLY plan shown -- a single 'Environmental Systems Engineering, B.S. at All Campuses' plan, matching the shape ENVSYS-2026.json also builds. Verified against the page's own printed subtotal: 'Total Credits 128' -- matches this file's item sum of 128. Two genuine, citable differences from the 2026 file, confirmed by diffing the raw suggested-plan HTML of both archived years directly (not assumed identical): (1) 2025's Year 2 Spring slot is a single straight requirement -- 'EME 210 (Take through DLC if not at UP)' -- with no ENGL 202C alternative; 2026 instead prints a conditional swap ('EME 210 (if at UP) or ENGL 202C (GWS) (if not at UP)' in Year 2 Spring, and the mirror-image swap in Year 3 Spring) that does not exist yet on the 2025-26 page. Since this file models a University Park student (the file's own campus scope, matching 2026's), the 2025 plan's un-conditioned EME 210 + ENGL 202C (one in each of Year 2 Spring and Year 3 Spring, same as 2026's UP-branch resolution) produces the identical net course list to 2026 for a UP student regardless of the conditional wording only 2026 added. (2) 2025 lists MATH 251 without the '#' Entrance-to-Major-requirement marker that some other prescribed courses on this page carry (cosmetic bulletin footnote difference, not a course-list change) -- noted for completeness, not modeled as a plan difference. As with ENVSYS-2022/2023/2024.json, CHEM 110's and EME 210's real prereq is MATH 22 (catalogs/chem_catalog.json, catalogs/eme_catalog.json -- not year-specific data), which itself chains through MATH 21, MATH 4, and MATH 3, none of which are in the bulletin's own suggested plan; MATH 3/4/21/22 are added as explicit Semester 1 items here for the same reason documented in ENVSYS-2026.json's own notes (clears every 'Could not schedule' warning, at the cost of pushing the real critical path past 8 terms -- see this repo's self-verification results for this major).",
